    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Como este painel funciona",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "O Node-RED grava no **InfluxDB** (aba *InfluxDB*, ou publicando por MQTT em `lab/sensor/+`). O Grafana **lê** o mesmo bucket `lab` e desenha. Ninguém liga um no outro em tempo real: o banco é o ponto de encontro.\n\nO *data source* já vem configurado em **Connections → Data sources → InfluxDB** (`http://influxdb:8086`, org `lab`, linguagem Flux). Gere dados na aba InfluxDB do Node-RED e clique em **Refresh** aqui."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Temperatura por sensor",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "influxdb",
        "uid": "P951FEA4DE68E13C5"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "influxdb",
            "uid": "P951FEA4DE68E13C5"
          },
          "query": "from(bucket: \"lab\")\n  |> range(start: v.timeRangeStart, stop: v.timeRangeStop)\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._measurement == \"leituras\" and r._field == \"temperatura\")\n  |> group(columns: [\"sensor\"])\n  |> aggregateWindow(every: v.windowPeriod, fn: mean, createEmpty: false)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "displayName": "${__field.labels.sensor}",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      }
    },
